<p>Phase 4 represents the long-range vision for SR-177 north of West Haven into Box Elder County. As of May 2026, this segment is in early-stage planning with no formal study or defined alignment.</p>

<hr class="divider">

<div class="section-label">Geographic Scope</div>
<h2>The Phase 4 Segment: 4000 South to Box Elder County Line</h2>

<p>Phase 4 extends the SR-177 corridor from the Phase 3 terminus (4000 South in West Haven) northward approximately 10–15 miles to the Box Elder County line. The segment passes through:</p>

<ul style="margin: 16px 0 20px 24px; line-height: 2.2;">
  <li><strong>West Haven (south end):</strong> 4000 South boundary</li>
  <li><strong>Unincorporated Weber County:</strong> Agricultural and open land between West Haven and Hooper</li>
  <li><strong>Hooper area (if applicable):</strong> Agricultural land with historic farming heritage</li>
  <li><strong>Unincorporated Weber County (north):</strong> Transition to Box Elder County</li>
</ul>

<p>The specific alignment, cities affected, and terminus point within Box Elder County have not been formally determined as of May 2026.</p>

